# 9. One correction I would make to the current research direction

The latest documents sometimes describe the next question as:

> “What is the earliest corpus-native Knowledge object?”

I agree, but I would make the research question slightly stronger:

$$
\boxed{
\textbf{What is the earliest corpus-native distinction between Knowledge, Knowledge-State, Fact, Evidence and Observation?}
}
$$

Because finding the first occurrence of `Knowledge` alone is insufficient.

The corpus already demonstrates that the same word can participate in radically different semantic constructions.

The real target is therefore:

```text
term occurrence
      ↓
conceptual role
      ↓
object identity
      ↓
semantic responsibility
      ↓
relations to neighbouring objects
      ↓
historical evolution
```

That is much more robust.

